Town names, echod/internal/feature/home/places.tsv.gz
  From GeoNames (https://www.geonames.org/), the cities5000 and cities15000 lists, licensed under
  the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 License (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
  Changes: reduced to places of 15,000 people or more, and of 5,000 or more in the U.S. and Canada;
  each kept as its name (in Latin letters where the screen's font has no others), latitude,
  longitude and population. The rain map credits GeoNames on screen. tools/places/make_places.py
  makes the file from GeoNames' download.

Radar color tables, echod/internal/feature/home/radar_palettes.go
  The colors RainViewer's API documentation publishes for each radar reflectivity
  (https://www.rainviewer.com/files/rainviewer_api_colors_table.csv), and the palette of the Iowa
  Environmental Mesonet's national composite, used to read their tiles back into reflectivity.
